# Add this line to the droplet's existing crontab (crontab -e) alongside
# the tri-cities-7day-forecast and western-us-noaa-outlooks lines already
# there. Needs the same WB_API_KEY already exported at the top of that
# crontab (WindBorne account/key, shared across every project that uses it
# -- no new key needed here).
#
# Runs every 3 hours at :50 (00:50, 03:50, 06:50, ... 21:50 UTC) -- chosen
# over hourly, since WM-6 forecasts don't meaningfully change enough run to
# run at a single point to justify 24 renders/day across 9 cities; :50 as
# a buffer before the top of the next hour, unlike the SPC/IEM buffer in
# western-us-noaa-outlooks, this hasn't been empirically checked against a
# live cycle boundary. Worth confirming against a few real days of
# state/publish.log (does the forecast's own "init" timestamp actually
# advance every run, or does it sometimes still show a stale cycle?) and
# adjusting if it's off.
#
# Before the first run: seed each location's climatology cache once --
#   cd /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart
#   venv/bin/python3 deploy/seed_climatology.py
# publish_charts.py will hard-fail any location whose cached climatology
# file is missing, rather than silently skipping the climatology overlay.

50 0,3,6,9,12,15,18,21 * * * /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart/venv/bin/python3 /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart/deploy/publish_charts.py >> /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart/state/cron.log 2>&1
